1. Nominal Scale (नाम मात्र)
Definition

Data ko sirf categories (groups) me divide karta hai. Isme koi order nahi hota.

Characteristics
Qualitative data
Sirf naming/classification
No ranking
No arithmetic operations
Examples
Gender (Male, Female)
Blood Group (A, B, AB, O)
Religion
Eye Color
City Name
Statistics Allowed
Frequency
Percentage
Mode

2. Ordinal Scale (क्रम)
Definition

Data ko categories me divide karta hai aur order/ranking bhi hoti hai, lekin categories ke beech difference equal nahi hota.

Characteristics
Ranking possible
Difference between ranks unknown
No meaningful addition/subtraction
Examples
Class Rank (1st, 2nd, 3rd)
Satisfaction Level
Poor
Average
Good
Excellent
Education Level
Medal (Gold, Silver, Bronze)
Statistics Allowed
Median
Mode
Percentile

Interval Scale (अंतराल)
Definition

Order bhi hota hai aur equal intervals bhi hote hain, lekin true zero nahi hota.

Characteristics
Equal difference between values
Zero does NOT mean absence
Addition and subtraction possible
Multiplication/division not meaningful
Examples
Temperature in Celsius
Temperature in Fahrenheit
Calendar Year
IQ Score
Statistics Allowed
Mean
Median
Mode
Standard Deviation
Variance

4. Ratio Scale (अनुपात)
Definition

Sabse powerful scale.

Isme:

Categories
Order
Equal intervals
True zero

Sab present hote hain.

Characteristics
True zero exists
All mathematical operations possible
Examples
Height
Weight
Age
Income
Distance
Time
Number of Students
Statistics Allowed
Mean
Median
Mode
Standard Deviation
Variance
Geometric Mean
Harmonic Mean


